  "raw": {
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Business-Development-and-Project-Manager_R000024353": {
      "title": "Business Development and Project Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSalary Package: $126,306 to $140,543 p.a. (HEW Level 8) plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading Appointment Type:  Full Time Continuing Location: Based onsite at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde If you are a natural relationship-builder who enjoys negotiating with international stakeholders, closing deals and ensuring projects are delivered to a high standard, then this role, operating in a fast-paced environment, may be for you. The Role The Macquarie University College EMI Centre has a range of courses and programs that require both strategic business development (promoting, recruiting, converting new business and building client relationships) and operational delivery ( logistics coordination, delivery of operational requirements and project oversight). This role sits at the intersection of both business development and operational delivery and requires confidence across both areas. Reporting to the Director of the College, you will be the trusted first point of contact for new and long-term partners – responsible not only for identifying and securing new business but for ensuring it is delivered to a high standard from enquiry through to completion. You will act as the conduit between the College, the wider University recruitment teams, and external stakeholders, moving fluidly between strategic conversations and operation execution. Key responsibilities for the role: Business Development Identify, pursue and convert new business opportunities, including managing and growing our online resources — IELTSonline.com, the Fundamentals of Teaching EMI Microcredential, and the English for STEM program suite. Prepare and deliver compelling proposals, quotations and business cases that build trust and secure prospective business. Negotiate commercial terms with international and domestic stakeholders and build long-term partnerships that support strategic growth. Liaise with University recruitment and marketing teams on collateral, website content, promotion and product brand compliance to support conversion. Operations and Project Delivery Scope, plan and report on projects to inform and support strategic decision-making. Support the implementation of projects, including tracking milestones, deliverables and evaluation outcomes. Coordinate the end-to-end delivery and logistics of visiting student and educator groups, ensuring smooth, well-run and memorable training and cultural experiences. Manage payments and administrative processes associated with client relationships and project delivery. Build and manage relationships with project teams, and internal and external stakeholders, to ensure operational requirements are consistently met. General Comply with relevant EEO and WHS regulations Perform any other duties as required and appropriate for this classification. About Us Macquarie University College provides local and international students with alternative pathway programs to undergraduate and postgraduate degrees through our accelerated face-to-face learning model. The College delivers Foundation, Intensive, Diplomas, UniReady and Masters Qualifying programs, English language programs, and operates the Pearson Testing Centre on campus. The EMI Centre sits within the College. This is an exciting opportunity to join a dynamic team committed to supporting student success. About You You are someone who genuinely enjoys business development and operational delivery. You will have demonstrated knowledge and success in growing and maintaining business products both internationally and domestically, with the confidence and skill to negotiate contracts, sell products, and present to small and large groups. On the operations side, you'll bring strong project coordination skills, high levels of accuracy, and the ability to manage competing deadlines without compromising quality. You will have high-level written and verbal communication skills and excellent interpersonal skills, enabling you to work collaboratively with teams across the University and with international stakeholders from diverse backgrounds. You will be skilled in the use of the Microsoft suite of products, and comfortable moving between strategic and operational tasks. To Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter (no more than 2 pages) that outlines how you meet the selection criteria below: Selection Criteria: An undergraduate degree, preferably in business, marketing, international relations or equivalent experience. Demonstrated success identifying, pursuing and converting new business opportunities in an international context. Proven experience building and sustaining relationships with international stakeholders, including negotiating commercial terms and navigating cross-cultural communication with confidence and professionalism Demonstrated experience in delivering complex multi-stakeholder projects, including planning, coordinating logistics, tracking milestones and evaluating outcomes for for small or large groups. Proficiency in administrative and digital skills. Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office suite and experience with online education products. Excellent time management skills and high attention to detail, with a demonstrated ability to manage multiple concurrent projects and competing deadlines without compromising quality. * Work hours may vary from time to time to accommodate business needs. The expectation is that staff will be on campus most workdays. This role requires a National Police Check Clearance and applicants are preferred to hold a current Working with Children Check (WWCC) or be willing to obtain one. Note: This position is not available for visa sponsorship, and the successful applicant must have valid work rights in Australia. Specific Role Enquiries:  Please contact Akina Banh, Administration Officer ( akina.banh@mq.edu.au ) Application Close: Thursday, 24 September 2026, 23:59pm Interviews are expected to be conducted face-to-face on Friday, 2 October 2026, in the morning. Please ensure you are available on this day. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 24/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Student-Programs-Officer_R000024384": {
      "title": "Student Programs Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n• Annual base salary from $102,136 - $112,741 (HEW Level 6) plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading • Appointment type: Full time, continuing • Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal campus, North Ryde We are seeking a passionate and self-motivated individual to provide operational and administrative support to the Inclusion and Belonging portfolio in the delivery, governance, and continuous improvement of student groups, including oversight of approximately 130 student clubs and societies. The role supports event coordination, stakeholder engagement, risk management, and process improvement. This is a campus-based (on-site) , student-facing role that offers the opportunity to make a meaningful and lasting impact on the University community. Key Accountabilities: Provide project, administrative and event coordination and support to the Inclusion and Belonging team. Coordinate student group events and other major student-facing activities, including managing registrations, coordinating rosters and training, arranging speaker briefings and facilitating venue and facilities bookings. Support the induction, engagement and ongoing development of student leaders and representatives involved in student clubs and societies at university wide level. Provide coordination and administration support to student groups, including as record keeping, budget monitoring, financial administration, scheduling, and other administrative requirements. Research and collate information to support the development of strategic goals of student commencement and transition. Review and maintain the student groups website and social media channels, including content development. Undertake reviews and evaluate all student clubs and their activities to support continuous improvement and alignment with Macquarie University’s governance frameworks, policies and regulatory obligations. About You You’ll be a self-starting individual with excellent work organisation and time management skills and ability to remain resilient when under pressure. You will have expert planning, design and content development capabilities, able to effectively communicate with stakeholders at all levels. You will enjoy working in a dynamic environment, applying a methodical and consultative approach in your work, and be motivated to deliver work outputs that are of a consistent high quality.   How to Apply To be considered for this position, please apply online and attach your resume and a separate cover letter that outlines how you meet the selection criteria below: Degree or equivalent experience in business, education, finance, law or related discipline. Knowledge of tertiary students and the Australian higher education system. Understanding of first-year experience, transition, and peer support models within higher education, with the ability to apply these within university frameworks. Demonstrated experience coordinating major and complex student engagement projects, events and programs. Proven ability to mentor or supervise volunteers or student leaders High level written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare clear documentation, communications, and reports. Demonstrated ability to balance compliance, risk management and student engagement outcomes within complex or high-volume operational environments.       Applications Close: 20th September 2026 at 11:59pm (AEST)   Please note we reserve the right to progress or decline an application as well as close the advertisement prior to the stated closing date. Why Join Us? Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation in 1964, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community.  Connect with us today . We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University. 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Extensive training and professional development programs Onsite childcare facilities to support working parents Onsite vacation care during school holidays Discounted health insurance Subsidised membership at our Sport & Aquatic Centre Access to an Employee Assistance Program for free and confidential support Convenient onsite GP, imaging, and physiotherapy clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 20/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
