    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Postdoctoral-Fellow_R000024286": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n- Salary package:  $112,550 - $120,621 (A.6-A.8) per annum plus 17% employer's superannuation and annual leave loading  - Appointment Type: Full-time, fixed term appointment for 2 years  - Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde  The role    We are seeking a Postdoc toral Fellow, to join our category theory group. This position is associated with Dr. Jean-Simon Pacaud Lemay's AFOSR grant FA9550-24-1-0008. As such, the successful applicant will work in the area of differential categories, tangent categories, and other category theory related topics, whether th is be for mathematics (such as for differential geometry, algebraic geometry, etc.) or for computer science (such as machine learning, linear logic, etc.).    While the position start date is flexible, the successful applicant must have completed their PhD prior to commencing the role. The position can commence at any time during 2027, with the appointment being for a period of two years from the successful applicant’s commencement date.   About you (Selection Criteria)   PhD (or soon completed a PhD) in mathematics, computer science, or related areas.    Research experience in, related to, or applications of category theory.    Why Join Us?   Macquarie is a university engaged with the real and often complex problems and opportunities that define our lives. Since our foundation over 60 years ago, we have aspired to be a different type of university. Over the years, we have grown to become the centre of a vibrant local and global community. Connect with us today .   We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Take a look at the fabulous staff benefits on offer when you work at Macquarie University.   How to Apply To be considered, please apply online and submit :    A Cover Letter, which includes the name of two references and, if applicable, the expected end date of your PhD.   Your Resume   A r esearch proposal, 3-page max (excluding references).   *This position requires a criminal history and qualifications check.   Applications Close: Friday 16 th of October at 11:59pm (AEST) 2026.  We welcome applications from international candidates.  For enquiries or a confidential conversation:   P lease contact JS Lemay – Senior Lecturer at js.lemay@mq.edu.au .     The Faculty of Science and Engineering at Macquarie University has a goal to increase the engagement of women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people from diverse backgrounds in STEMM roles. Applications are considered holistically, and candidates are encouraged to apply even if their experience does not meet each individual selection criterion.   Pre-Employment Checks    Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will  be required  to  participate  in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for.    Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University.  If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 16/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/School-Administration-Officer_R000024181": {
      "title": "School Administration Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n· Salary package: From $102,136 (HEW Level 6.1) per annum plus 17% employer's superannuation contribution and annual leave loading. · Appointment Type: Full-time, fixed term role till 3rd August 2027 · Location: Based at Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde The Role The Faculty of Science and Engineering is seeking an agile and proactive Administration Officer for an immediate start. If you thrive in a busy environment and enjoy supporting a diverse range of stakeholders, this could be the ideal opportunity for you. As part of the School Operations team, you will play a key role in delivering high-quality financial, administrative and customer service support to the School of Mathematical and Physical Sciences. Reporting to the School Operations Manager, you will bring a strong service mindset, excellent organisational skills, and the ability to work independently while adapting to changing priorities. You will support a broad range of operational activities across financial administration, staff and student support, and contribute to initiatives that enhance the School's effectiveness and performance. Some of your key responsibilities include: Coordinate and administer School-level processes across the full employee lifecycle, including recruitment, onboarding, leave and termination, together with visiting and honorary appointments and the academic workload database, applying University policies, procedures and systems. Prepare and monitor financial reporting for the School/Department portfolios on expenditure against budgets and project accounts, contribute to annual budget preparation, and coordinate purchasing, procurement and travel administration for staff. Gather, analyse and interpret data and information to prepare reports and recommendations that inform School decision-making and meet internal and external reporting requirements. Develop and maintain effective relationships with internal and external stakeholders, and interpret and apply University and Faculty policies, processes and systems within the School, liaising with shared services and business partners as required. Contribute to the review and improvement of HR, finance and administrative systems and processes; comply with relevant professional standards, EEO and WHS regulations; and undertake other duties appropriate to the classification as required. About Us The Faculty of Science and Engineering is a young and dynamic faculty driven by the spirit of discovery. Here we nurture the next generation of science and technology innovators. From a handful of students on the University’s first day, the faculty now serves nearly 6000 students across all our programs. The School of Mathematical and Physical Science is an inclusive community in scientific collaboration. Mathematics and statistics drive breakthroughs in technology and data science, while physics and astronomy seek to understand matter and the Universe – everything from quarks to galaxy clusters. We collaborate closely with local, national, and international organisations and companies across the diverse mathematical and physical sciences fields. Further information about our school is available here . To Apply To be considered for this role, please apply online by submitting a current CV and a cover letter addressing the selection criteria (maximum two pages). Please provide specific examples demonstrating how your skills, knowledge and experience meet each criterion. Applications that do not address the selection criteria may not be considered. Selection Criteria A degree in business administration or a related discipline, and/or equivalent relevant experience. Strong organisational, stakeholder relationship and communication skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deliver to tight deadlines. Knowledge and experience working in a complex administrative environment, preferably in a complex organisation. Knowledge of financial and budgeting principles. Intermediate skills in Microsoft Office and database systems, and the ability to quickly learn new systems and technology. Experience in contributing to administrative process improvement. *** The successful candidate will also be required to complete a police check. Note: Applicants must hold valid Australian work rights for the duration of this appointment. Role-specific Enquiries: Theresa Han, School / Department Operations Manager at Theresa.Han@mq.edu.au Applications Close:   Sunday 13 September 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEST) *** Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and we reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. We also reserve the right to close the advertisement early if a sufficient number of qualified applicants is received. Why work at Macquarie We rank amongst the top employers in the Australian Workplace Employers Index, having recently earned a five-star rating in the QS World Rankings with the highest rating for employability. Our prime location is just a short walk from Macquarie University Metro Station and Macquarie Shopping Centre. Enjoy the benefits of working at a campus that offers: 17% Superannuation Subsidised onsite parking options Flexible working options Training and professional development Onsite childcare facilities Discounted health insurance (Medibank) Onsite vacation care Employee Assistance Program Subsidised membership at the Sport & Aquatic Centre Onsite GP, imaging & physio clinics Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 13/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Research-Fellow_R000024316": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - China Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-29\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nShape Australia's understanding of contemporary China and pursue impactful research and inform national policy conversations. · Salary Package: From Level A.1 ($89,579) to A.6 ($112,550) per annum, plus 17% superannuation and annual leave loading. · Full-time, fixed-term (12-month residential position) · Macquarie University, Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde About the Fellowship The China Strategic Knowledge Initiative at Macquarie University invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Fellowship commencing in 2027. This is a12-month, residential position based at Macquarie University in Sydney designed to support emerging scholars whose research informs Australia’s understanding of contemporary China. There will be two additional 12-month fellowships available in the future, one in 2028 and one in 2029. This fellowship is intended to strengthen policy-relevant scholarship and public engagement on China’s foreign policy, security, defence, and domestic politics. The successful candidate will contribute to research excellence while actively engaging and informing government, media, and the broader policy community. This fellowship offers a unique opportunity for an early-career scholar to develop a strong research profile while contributing to Australia’s public and policy conversations on China. Eligible applicants with a demonstrated commitment to scholarly excellence and public engagement are strongly encouraged to apply. About the Role Based in the Faculty of Arts at Macquarie University in Sydney, you will join a vibrant intellectual community with access to the University's research resources, working under the mentorship and guidance of Associate Professor Courtney Fung, PhD, and Honorary Professor Bates Gill, PhD. The fellowship is structured across two areas: - 80% Research (approximately four days per week): Independent and joint research aligned with the Initiative's mission. You will be expected to make significant progress in refining and publishing the results of your PhD thesis research. - 20% Engagement (approximately one day per week): Public and policy engagement activities, planned in consultation with your fellowship advisors. These may include: Policy briefings and consultations Policy papers and opinion pieces Media commentary and public outreach Participation in workshops, seminars, and public events Contributions to Australian policy discussions regarding China Eligibility: Applications are open to Australian citizens and permanent residents. You must be able to live and work in Australia for the duration of the fellowship. About Us Established in 2026, the China Strategic Knowledge Initiative is supported by the National Foundation for Australia-China Relations and Macquarie University. It aims to build Australia's knowledge base and policy engagement on China through rigorous scholarship and meaningful public outreach. More information about CSKI and the fellowship program is available at https://www.mq.edu.au/faculty-of-arts/schools/school-of-international-<br>studies/our-research/china-strategic-knowledge-initiative. About You (Selection Criteria) You are an early-career scholar with a demonstrated commitment to scholarly excellence and public engagement, ready to develop a strong research profile and help shape Australia's understanding of contemporary China. You bring rigour to your research and enthusiasm for sharing your expertise with government, media, and the wider policy community. A completed PhD (or thesis submitted) relevant to contemporary China studies, with the capacity to refine and publish results. Exemplary scholarly achievement and strong future promise in one or more areas of contemporary China studies: Chinese foreign policy and international relations; security and defence issues; and/or Chinese domestic politics. A clear commitment to public engagement, including the readiness to brief government, business and the broader policy community. Experience or willingness to engage in media appearances, policy writing, and opinion writing. Willingness to take part in public-facing activities such as workshops, seminars, and public events. Excellent English-language communication skills, both written and spoken. Professional integrity and collegiality, including high standards of reliability, decorum, and joint work. *** The successful candidate will be required to complete a Police Check, an academic qualification check and any other relevant background checks required for the role. Application Requirements Applicants must submit an application package online including: 1. Letter of Application (maximum two pages) summarising the applicant’s interest in the fellowship, detail relevant qualifications and research agenda and confirm Australian citizenship or Australian permanent residency status. 2. Curriculum vitae which prrovides candidate's current contact information and details academic credentials, professional experience, research and publication record. 3. References which include the names, title(s), and email of three persons who can knowledgeably speak to the candidate's academic qualifications and professional character. One of the references must be the candidate's primary PhD advisor. Additional supporting documentation may be requested from shortlisted candidates. Application Timeline: Applications Close: Thursday15 October 2026 at 11:59 p.m. (AEDT) Shortlisted candidates contacted: November 2026 Successful candidate notified: December 2026 Position commences: 2027 (prior to 1 June 2027, date to be agreed) For general enquiries about the role, please contact the Mirna Alaaiddin at mirna.alaaiddin@mq.edu.au We reserve the right to progress or decline an application prior to the application closing date. Pre-Employment Checks Macquarie University cultivates a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity. Prior to completion of an offer of employment, preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. Your employment is conditional upon the completion and maintenance of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 15/10/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
