    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/Student-Ambassador_R000024250": {
      "title": "Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nPart time\n\n- $46.03 per hour (HEW Level 2) + 12% superannuation.   - Casual roles based at Wallumattagal Campus, North Ryde.   - Seeking current domestic MQ students The Role     Student Ambassadors are carefully selected representatives of Macquarie University. As the face of the University for prospective students, ambassadors are chosen for their communication skills, professionalism, leadership   potential   and engagement with university life.   We’re   looking for current Macquarie University students who make the most of their university experience and are excited to share it with others. Whether   you’ve   been involved in student clubs or societies, sport, mentoring, leadership programs, volunteering, PACE, internships,   exchange   or other university initiatives,   we’d   love to hear how   you’ve   contributed to campus life.   As a Student   Ambassador   you’ll   gain more than casual employment.   Join a highly regarded team of student leaders who   represent   Macquarie, develop career-defining   skills   and help future students discover   what's   possible.   Depending on your interests and experience, you may have opportunities to feature in university marketing campaigns, videos, publications,   and   social media content . The main activities you would be performing as a student ambassador include:   Sharing your Macquarie story through presentations, webinars and conversations with future students,   parents   and teachers   Helping future students navigate their options and make confident decisions about university study   Contributing to social media content and digital campaigns that inspire future students to see themselves at Macquarie   Captur ing   prospective student details (leads) at student recruitment events and activities.     Represent ing   Macquarie University at careers markets , expos and other major events including those hosted by faculties or other Macquarie departments   Conduct ing   tours of the Macquarie University campus   Provid ing   event support   including set up, registration and other activities for in-person and online recruitment activities   Conduct ing outbound   telephone calling to prospective students or other stakeholders   Support ing   the Future Students team with administrative & office tasks   as   required   Handl ing of   boxes of approximately 10kg on a regular basis   Driv ing   University vehicles in a safe manner to various student recruitment events (on and off campus).       To perform well in this role, you will need to be approachable, proactive, adaptable, confident in   presenting to   a wide range of audiences and willing to go the extra mile.    Many of our Student Ambassadors have gone on to secure competitive graduate positions across consulting, government, education, health,   technology   and finance. Alumni   frequently   identify   their ambassador experience as one of the most valuable opportunities for developing confidence,   communication   and leadership skills.     Perks   of the role:     Build sought-after professional skills in communication, presentation,   networking   and stakeholder engagement   Develop confidence speaking with audiences ranging from individual students to large groups   Connect with senior university staff, industry   guests   and students from across the university   Gain valuable experience that strengthens internship and graduate job applications   Be considered for opportunities to feature in university campaigns, videos,   publications   and digital content   Join a supportive ambassador community and form lasting friendships and professional networks   Represent Macquarie at flagship events including Open Day, Experience Macquarie Days,   schools   visits, expos and careers markets and other major recruitment activities   Earn a competitive hourly rate while making a meaningful impact on future students         You must be available for Open Day on   Saturday   14   August,   2027   and training days throughout   2026 and 2027 .         * This position requires a Working with Children Check Clearance. You must hold,   or can   obtain, a   paid   Working with Children Check (not Volunteer version), should an offer of employment be made. For more information see:   https://ocg.nsw.gov.au/working-children-check To Apply     Ready to become a Student Ambassador?     To be considered, please complete the following steps:   Step 1: Submit your application online. Click the Apply button to upload your current resume   to Workday. Step 2: C omplete th e   survey.       SA 2027 Recruitment Survey – Fill out form   (https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/KHY8Lq0vhq)     The survey will give you an opportunity to tell us about your experiences, involvement at   university   and how you meet the criteria below.     We're   looking for students who:   Are currently enrolled at Macquarie University with   ideally   at least   two years of study   remaining .   Demonstrate strong organisational and time management skills.   Are confident communicators who can connect with a wide range of audiences.   Enjoy helping others and providing   accurate , helpful information.   Act with professionalism, integrity and accountability when   representing   Macquarie University.   Can work independently and contribute positively within a team environment.   Are available to work across weekdays, evenings and weekends as   required , including major university events.   Hold a current Australian driver's licence (P1, P2 or Full) and are comfortable travelling to events across metropolitan and regional locations.     Highly regarded   While not essential, we would love to hear about your experience in any of the following areas:   Customer service, hospitality, retail, tutoring, mentoring or other people-focused roles.   Presenting,   facilitating   or public speaking.   Developing content for social media or digital platforms.   Leadership,   volunteering   or community involvement.   Participation in university life through student groups, sport, PACE, exchange, mentoring programs, volunteering, leadership   initiatives   or other extracurricular activities.   Experience using Microsoft Office applications including Word,   Excel   and PowerPoint.     Step 3: Show us your story   Student Ambassadors are storytellers,   communicators   and connectors.   Submit a video   (no longer than 2 minutes)   introducing yourself and speaking   about   the following topics:   Why did you choose Macquarie University?   What do you enjoy most about your degree?   What has been your most memorable experience at Macquarie?     Please  upload your  video to   this   Dropbox folder     https://www.dropbox.com/request/sp2k1amh52vjilwu7iyx     Role-specific Enquiries:   Domestic Student Recruitment team via   domesticSArecruitment@mq.edu.au     General Enquiries:   Email the Positions and Appointments team via   positionsandappointments@mq.edu.au       Applications Close:  27 September 2026   at 11:59pm (AEST)      If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 27/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
