    "https://mq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/CareersatMQ/job/Wallumattagal-Campus-Macquarie-University/F-B-attendant_R000023498": {
      "title": "F&B attendant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nTo provide and ensure the highest standard of service to all customers and staff by performing the duties listed below in a highly efficient, effective and professional manner while adhering to all rules, policies and procedures. THE ROLE Engaging customers, new and regulars, in a fast-paced environment Working in a fun team and make sure our customers are happy ones, that have positive things to say about you and their café experience Running daily operation in the venue including coffee making and food prepare. Providing a wide variety of food & beverage on campus. Able to keep eye on food and beverage quality and overview the venue to maintain high stand performance. Able to work as role model to your peers. ABOUT YOU Must have minimum 1 - 2 years wait staff experience in a high volume, fast paced café or food and beverage outlet Right attitude - enthusiastic, know how to have fun, personable, the first thing people notice about you is your smile and welcoming energy Customer satisfaction - you'll go above and beyond to get the work done and make sure your customers are HAPPY Understanding of laws as they relate to the organisation HACCP/Food Safety and WHS laws. Able to work rotating 7 days roster, in accordance with business needs and requirements. ABOUT US Within U@MQ, the Campus Services team operate multiple hospitality & retail venues providing products, services and events to students, staff and community members across the University campus. Our services include managing and operating Café’s, Licensed Bar, Vending, Academic Dress, Branded Merchandise and delivering events and activations across campus. Benefits at U@MQ Fun and collaborative values-driven culture Access to discounted health insurance Professional development and career progression opportunities Access to the Macquarie University Library (borrowing, printing and data bases) Rostered days off available If you are passionate and experienced, want to work in a fun, friendly and fast paced environment, apply now to start ASAP! How to Apply To be considered for this position, please submit your CV and short cover letter outlining your suitability for the role as part of the online application process. All applicants must have the right to work in Australia. If you're already part of the Macquarie Group (MQ University, U@MQ, MQ Health, MGSM), you'll need to apply through your employee Workday account. To apply for this job: Login to Workday and go to the Careers App > Find Jobs. Applications Close: 29/09/2026 11:59 PM ​ A Place Where You Belong At Macquarie, we believe diversity makes us stronger, inclusion drives our success, and belonging inspires us to do our best work. We are proud to foster a community where different backgrounds, identities, and experiences are valued, and where our people are empowered to thrive through supportive leadership, shared responsibility, and a deep commitment to genuine care and respect for our community. Find out more about our vision for a truly inclusive workplace in our Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Framework . Flexible Work At Macquarie, we believe by providing flexibility in when, where and how work is done, we can support our staff to manage their personal commitments, while optimising their work performance and contributions to the University. See how we lead in flexible work to enable an outcome focused and inclusive workplace. To learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit our Jobs at Macquarie page."
    },
